^SAMPLE = GSM2367503
!Sample_title = Sequencing of the plasmid sgRNA library_lane 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2367503
!Sample_status = Public on Jul 17 2017
!Sample_submission_date = Nov 01 2016
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = A549 Cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample type: plasmid sgRNA library
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were transduced with sgRNA lentivirus and subsequently infected with influenza A virus (PR8 strain).
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Cells were grown under standard laboratory conditions and stably transfected with CRISPR components.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were sorted via flow cytometry, genomic DNA was extracted, and PCR for the sgRNA sequences was performed.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Illumina adaptors and barcodes were incorporated into the PCR primers.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = PCR amplified libraries were generated with independent barcodes to allow multiplexing.  50% PhiX DNA was included in the sequencing run, as low diversity libraries were expected.
!Sample_description = Double Lane Sequencing
!Sample_description = HiSeq2000 Rapid Run
!Sample_description = Plasmid NH
!Sample_data_processing = The sgRNA reads (which had 5' and 3' flanking regions that matched the sgRNA expression lentivirus vector) were quality filtered and mapped to a reference table of sgRNA sequences provided in Konermann et al, Nature 2015 (supplementary table 6).
!Sample_data_processing = Read numbers were normalized by dividing by the total read depth to give a percentage of total reads (displayed in the "percentage of reads" column in the processed data tables).
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Raw and normalized read numbers
